  "description": "Section 232 tariffs on patented pharmaceuticals and active pharmaceutical ingredients (APIs), including key starting materials. Annex I codes face a 100% ad valorem rate for all countries not covered by a preferential arrangement (this includes all African countries). Annex IV codes are explicitly subject to a Section 232 zero tariff and are also exempt from the Section 122 surcharge per Proclamation 11012.",
  "proclamation": "Proclamation 11020, signed April 2, 2026; Federal Register April 9, 2026 (FR Doc 2026-06956)",
  "legal_authority": "Section 232 of the Trade Expansion Act of 1962, 19 U.S.C. 1862",
  "rate": 1.0,
  "effective_date": "July 31, 2026 (companies in Annex III); September 29, 2026 (all other companies)",
  "note": "Rate applies to patented pharmaceutical articles (Annex I). Generics are explicitly excluded. EU/Japan/South Korea/Switzerland: 15%; UK: 10%+column-1 rate. Companies with approved onshoring plans: 20% (rising to 100% on April 2, 2030). Annex IV codes (zero rate under Section 232) are listed in the exceptions field.",
